Subject: [PATCH 06921/11362] [outer-loop] ka59: L7 SOLVED, FULL GAME CLEAR
 (round 9, codex)

Round-9 gpt-5.6-sol session reproduced round 8's two upper-stack
relocations and first plus launch in 38 calls, then found the second
plus interaction needs no further cycling-stack launch: routing the
horizontal helper to x=6-11,y=21-23 and pressing ACTION2 strikes the
plus's bar with the helper's lower edge, launching the plus downward
directly into its matching target. The plus can be solved before
either helper is finally socketed. levels_completed advanced from 6
to 7 with GameState.WIN.

The complete winning L7 tail is only 93 actions, well inside the
level's own 200-action internal counter -- round 8's stopping point
was a budget/pacing issue, not a difficulty wall.

The source agent's own reproduction_verified is honestly false
(budget ran out after the win), but the outer loop independently
re-verified regardless: 5x fresh env.reset() + replay via a new
resolver priority branch (ka59's special extended-label apply
function, handling both bare-digit and click-coordinate labels), all
5 confirmed level=7, state=GameState.WIN. ka59 is fully solved.

ops/arc_solve_registry.yaml: ka59 levels_reproduced 6 -> 7,
full_game_clear: true, final_game_state: GameState.WIN.
reproducible_total_levels 168 -> 169 (sum-checked;
arc_count_integrity_lint exit 0).

